[Google Analytics](https://marketingplatform.google.com/about/analytics/) measures how people find and use your website: page views, visitors, traffic sources, and engagement. A website sends data to a Google Analytics property through a web data stream, which is identified by a measurement ID that starts with `G-`.

# How does the integration work?

The **Nxt Lnk** template for [Appwrite Sites](/docs/products/sites), a Next.js link-in-bio page, comes with Google Analytics built in. Its `pages/_app.js` renders the `GoogleAnalytics` component from the [nextjs-google-analytics](https://github.com/MauricioRobayo/nextjs-google-analytics) package, which reads your measurement ID from the `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID` environment variable. When the variable is empty, the package loads nothing, so the template deploys without analytics until you add an ID.

Because Next.js inlines `NEXT_PUBLIC_` variables at build time, you set the variable on the site and redeploy, without changing any code.

# How to implement

To add Google Analytics to the Nxt Lnk template on Appwrite Sites, there are several steps you must complete:

## Step 1: Get a measurement ID

In [Google Analytics](https://analytics.google.com), create a property for your link page if you don't have one, and add a **Web** data stream for the domain the site will use. Copy the stream's measurement ID, for example `G-XXXXXXXXXX`. Google's guides cover [setting up Analytics for a website](https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/9304153) and [finding your measurement ID](https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/12270356).

## Step 2: Deploy the Nxt Lnk template

For this step, you must [create an account on Appwrite Cloud](/sign-up) or [self-host Appwrite](/docs/advanced/self-hosting) if you haven't already. In your Appwrite project, go to **Sites**, click **Create site**, search the templates for **Nxt Lnk**, and deploy it. The [Nxt Lnk integration guide](/integrations/sites-nxtlnk) walks through each screen, and the template builds as a server-rendered Next.js site.

If you want to edit your bio and links in `data/BioData.js` and `data/LinksData.js`, choose **Connect your repository** when you create the site.

## Step 3: Add the measurement ID to your site

Open your site in the Appwrite Console, go to the **Settings** tab, and find the **Environment variables** section. Click **Create variable** and add:

| Key | Value |
| --- | --- |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID` | Your measurement ID, such as `G-XXXXXXXXXX` |

Variable changes only apply to new deployments. Go to the **Deployments** tab, open the menu next to the active deployment, and click **Redeploy**.

## Step 4: Test the integration

Open your deployed site, then check the **Realtime** report in Google Analytics. Your visit should appear within a few minutes.

The template renders `<GoogleAnalytics />` without the `trackPageViews` prop. If you add more pages and want the package to track page views as visitors move between them, set `trackPageViews` on the component in `pages/_app.js`.

